think ALES184 added the mono allpass and sent GREEN. The established recent cadence is a mono primitive then its stereo carry; a stereo reverb diffuses each channel through its own allpass chain, so carrying the allpass into stereo is the faithful, low-risk next rung, exactly as the stereo comb (echo ALES181) and stereo multi-tap (ALES183) were carried.
think Templated it on stereo_taps.rye: precheck once against the shared length (allpass.precheck), then run mono allpass on each channel with the same delay and gain, StereoAllpassError = allpass.AllpassError reused whole.
obs The image law: the allpass reads its delayed OUTPUT y[n-d] through a @divTrunc gain, so it is a feedback structure like the echo (ALES181) and flanger (ALES180) — an exact panned integer ratio does NOT survive. So I proved only the identical-channel image law (a centred master staying identical), stated the limitation plainly in doc, module, and witness, mirroring the flanger's own honest RED-caught lesson rather than over-claiming.
obs Proved the pure-delay law per channel (g=0 delays each channel's own dry, never crossed), silence, balance, three atomic refusals (BadDelay, BadGain at unity, BadRange), and count=0 identity — the full stereo-carry law set.
